name: Calm operational failure reading before investigation commitment
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/source_baselines.py @TMP_TARGET @ART prepare @TMP_HOME
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/source_baselines.py @TMP_TARGET @ART dirty
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/operational_failure.py @TMP_TARGET @ART before
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 SETUP · READY THE MAP RUN | setup
submit: logs
require-live-snap: 20 LOGS | before-map-logs
expect-not: autonomy:
expect-not: Map 1/3
ask: Does opening Logs retain pre-investigation Setup posture without displaying journey or autonomy chrome?
submit: run coverage:sweep {"writeSkips":true}
wait: 0.5
submit: logs
keys: End
require-live-snap: 25 Cause: | failure-receipt
expect: dirty tree
expect: Details: failure
expect-not: fallback_context
expect-not: forbidden claims
expect-not: model <n>
expect-not: autonomy:
expect-not: Map 1/3
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/operational_failure.py @TMP_TARGET @ART after
ask: Does the operational failure lead with the cause and an explicit detail action, with full context retained in artifacts and no unrelated model hint?
submit: failure
require-live-snap: 20 FAILURE HANDOFF | full-failure-details
expect: coverage:sweep
expect: dirty tree
expect-not: autonomy:
expect-not: Map 1/3
submit: logs
keys: End
expect-echo-within: 300 keep-operational-draft
live-snap: retained-draft
resize: 160x48
live-snap: failure-160x48
expect: TARGET
expect-not: ENGAGEMENT
expect-not: · Map ·
resize: 96x89
live-snap: failure-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: failure-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: failure-60x20
resize: 40x12
live-snap: failure-40x12
expect: keep-operational-draft
expect-not: autonomy:
expect-not: Map 1/3
nav-mode:
keys: z
require-live-snap: 20 READ TRANSCRIPT | reader-40x12
keys: End PPage PPage
require-live-snap: 20 Cause: | reader-page-40x12
expect: dirty tree
ask: Can the operator read the cause through narrow transcript controls and resize across six sizes while retaining the draft?
keys: q
keys: C-_ Escape
require-live-snap: 15 keep-operational-draft | restored-draft
keys: C-c
require-live-snap: 10 CONFIRM SESSION EXIT | pre-map-quit
expect-not: autonomy:
expect-not: Map 1/3
keys: Escape
resize: 120x36
submit: setup
require-live-snap: 25 SETUP · READY THE MAP RUN | setup-return
expect-not: Map ✓
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/source_baselines.py @TMP_TARGET @ART after
keys: C-c
require-live-snap: 10 CONFIRM SESSION EXIT | explicit-quit
expect-not: autonomy:
expect-not: Map 1/3
keys: y
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 SETUP · READY THE MAP RUN | restarted
submit: failure
require-live-snap: 20 FAILURE HANDOFF | restarted-failure
expect: coverage:sweep
expect: dirty tree
expect-not: autonomy:
expect-not: Map 1/3
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/source_baselines.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/operational_failure.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
ask: Do Quit, Setup return and no-color restart preserve uncommitted posture and recover actual failure details without investigation work?
keys: C-c
require-live-snap: 10 CONFIRM SESSION EXIT | explicit-restart-quit
expect-not: autonomy:
expect-not: Map 1/3
keys: y
require-exit: 10
